WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.339 --> 00:00:03.006
(curious music)

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:06.140
- [Narrator] When Egypt's
Ministry of Health

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:09.080
issues its annual warning to
stay away from a dangerous

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.340
local delicacy called feseekh,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:13.579
you'd think people would comply.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:17.362
But for many, the risk
is worth the reward.

00:00:17.362 --> 00:00:20.029
(curious music)

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.324
If prepared poorly,

00:00:22.324 --> 00:00:26.503
feseekh can lead to
poisoning or even death.

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:31.720
Luckily, Ibrahim Shaheen
has been carefully preparing

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.683
this unique dish for decades.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.412
- [Narrator] Feseekh dates back to days

00:01:06.412 --> 00:01:07.900
when Egyptian pharaohs ruled the land.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.350
Each spring, the Nile River would recede

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:13.440
and the fish covered in sea
salt and sand were left behind

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.148
to rot on its shores.

00:01:15.148 --> 00:01:17.815
(curious music)

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.560
- [Narrator] Today it is
prepared a little differently.

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.860
The mullet fish are carefully
cleaned and sprayed with salt.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.960
They're then placed in
sterilized vats and left to cure

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.653
for up to 25 days.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.500
And when it's ready to
eat, the taste is ...

00:01:57.532 --> 00:02:00.023
(upbeat music)

00:02:00.023 --> 00:02:01.660
- [Narrator] But, despite its smell,

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:05.470
the fermented fish has become
a staple of Egyptian culture

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.370
and Ibrahim Shaheen is
proud to carry on making

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.373
this traditional dish
safe for all to enjoy.

00:02:38.466 --> 00:02:41.133
(upbeat music)

